{#
	Twig port of mod_pagepreview.html5.

	The identifier stays the flat legacy `mod_pagepreview`: this file sits in a
	bundle subdirectory with NO `.twig-root` marker anywhere under
	contao/templates/, so ContaoFilesystemLoader registers it under its bare
	basename rather than `modules/mod_pagepreview`. That is deliberate - the
	module's template is chosen by a DCA dropdown built from
	Controller::getTemplateGroup('mod_'), which throws on any identifier
	containing a slash.

	The .html5 was DELETED rather than kept alongside. Contao only renders the
	Twig surrogate when the highest-priority file for the identifier is not an
	.html5, so leaving both would silently keep rendering the old one.

	Escaping: Twig autoescapes, which is the point of the port. Anything that is
	genuinely markup rather than data is marked |raw and listed here so the next
	reader does not have to guess - cssID (a complete ` id="..."` attribute
	string), style, headline, and headerItems/bodyItems (rendered navigation).

	The `<!-- indexer::stop -->` / `<!-- indexer::continue -->` pair is DELIBERATE
	and was re-examined on 2026-09-05 rather than inherited. Contao\Search::indexPage()
	drops everything between them from tl_search, so this module's teasers are not
	indexed. Keep them:

	- This module renders OTHER pages' teasers. Unwrapped, the listing page would
	  win the search hit for a word that only appears in a linked page's teaser,
	  and the visitor would be sent to the index instead of to the page they were
	  looking for - which is already indexed on its own.
	- PagePreview extends ModuleNavigation, and core's own mod_navigation carries
	  exactly this wrapper (both the .html5 and the .html.twig).
	- It costs the site search no teaser text. asconsulting/contao-zyppy-search
	  reads page_teaser and page_image straight off the tl_page row in
	  ResultEnricher::enrich(), not out of the indexed body, so the wrapper decides
	  which page MATCHES and never what a result DISPLAYS.

	The one consequence, recorded rather than hidden: a teaser whose text appears
	nowhere on its own page is not searchable at all. The fix for that is to render
	the teaser on that page, not to unwrap a listing module.
#}
<!-- indexer::stop -->
<nav class="{{ class }} block"{{ cssID|default('')|raw }}{% if style %} style="{{ style|raw }}"{% endif %}{% if sliderItems|default(0) > 0 %} data-show="{{ sliderItems }}"{% endif %}>

	{% if headline %}
		<{{ hl }}>{{ headline|raw }}</{{ hl }}>
	{% endif %}

	<a href="{{ request }}#{{ skipId }}" class="invisible">{{ skipNavigation }}</a>

	<div class="header">
	{{ headerItems|default('')|raw }}
	</div>
	<div class="body">
	{{ bodyItems|default('')|raw }}
	</div>

	<a id="{{ skipId }}" class="invisible">&nbsp;</a>

</nav>
{% if sliderItems|default(0) > 0 %}
	{#
		Emitted from the module's own output rather than through TL_CSS/TL_JAVASCRIPT,
		which is the house pattern for front end modules in these packages. The
		published prefix is "page": it comes from the bundle class name (PageBundle)
		minus the "Bundle" suffix, NOT from the composer package name.

		jQuery is deliberately NOT loaded here. Contao ships it, but only puts it on
		the page when the layout has "Add jQuery" ticked, and nothing in PHP can
		reliably tell whether some other layout field or theme template has already
		loaded it. A second copy would break every plugin bound to the first, so
		page_slider.js warns in the console and stops instead. See README.md.
	#}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/bundles/page/css/page_slider.css">
<script src="/bundles/page/js/page_slider.js" defer></script>
{% endif %}
<!-- indexer::continue -->
